{title: I Want You To Know About Jesus}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

>Lyrics

(Drum and Piano Introduction for 12 Measures)

Verse 1

I am alive,

For I've received the grace of God

As my own.

I testify

No greater love or healing pow'r

Have I known...

Chorus 1

I want you to know about Jesus:

He took away my sin,

By grace, I'm born again.

For peace evermore, turn to Jesus,

The One who offers life without end!

Verse 2

The fear I knew

Was gone the day I gave the Lord

all control.

His Word is true:

The Living Water overflows

In my soul!

Chorus 2

I want you to know about Jesus:

There is no greater Friend;

Salvation is in Him.

For peace evermore, turn to Jesus;

Receive the life that never will end!

Bridge

Don't let this present world enslave you;

Call out to Jesus -- He will save you.

There's peace and comfort

Which the Lord alone can give.

The Shepherd's calling you,

So turn to Him and live!

Chorus 3

I want you to know about Jesus:

There is no greater Friend;

Salvation is in Him.

For peace evermore, turn to Jesus;

Receive the life that never will end,

Complete, redeeming pardon from sin,

And let the joy of heaven begin!
